# Real Estate Domain (Domain Pack)

## Entities

- **Property:** id, address, propertyType, bedrooms, bathrooms, squareFeet, yearBuilt, features, ownerId, version; PK/SK and GSI for by-owner
- **Listing:** propertyId, agentId, price, listingType, status, description, photos, publishedAt, expiresAt; GSI by agent, by status+time, by city+price
- **Lead:** propertyId, agentId, contact, source, status, message; GSI by agent, by createdAt
- **Agent:** id, brokerageId, profile; GSI by brokerage

## Single-Table Access Patterns

- Property by id: GetItem(PK=PROPERTY#id, SK=METADATA)
- Listings by property: Query(PK=PROPERTY#id, SK begins_with LISTING#)
- Listings by agent: Query(GSI1, GSI1PK=AGENT#id, GSI1SK begins_with LISTING#)
- Leads by agent: Query(GSI1, GSI1PK=AGENT#id, GSI1SK begins_with LEAD#)

## Domain Events

- **PropertyCreated,** **ListingPublished,** **LeadCaptured:** Use event envelope (eventId, eventType, aggregateId, payload, correlationId); publish to SNS/EventBridge; consumers (e.g. sync to OpenSearch, notifications) subscribe

## Business Rules

- One active listing per property (or enforce in service); listing status transitions; lead assignment; validate address and required fields at boundary

## Conventions

- Entities in single table with composite keys; events for cross-boundary communication; version for optimistic locking; see real-estate-events and real-estate-rules for detail

